---
const groups = [
  ["Articles", "a, an, the", "One unspecified thing, or a particular thing"],
  ["Demonstratives", "this, that, these, those", "Which item is near or further away"],
  ["Quantifiers", "some, many, few, every, several", "How many or how much"],
  ["Possessives", "my, your, his, her, its, our, their", "Whose"]
];
---

<div class="topic-sheet">
  <h1>Determiners - Specifying nouns</h1>
  <p>
    A <strong>determiner</strong> comes before a noun, and before any adjectives, to say which one, whose, or
    how many: <strong>the</strong> small dog; <strong>those</strong> three red balloons.
  </p>
  <section class="summary-block summary-rose">
    <h2>Four groups to recognise</h2>
    <table class="punct-table summary-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class="th-feature" scope="col">Group</th>
          <th class="th-rule" scope="col">Examples</th>
          <th class="th-example" scope="col">What it tells us</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          groups.map(([group, examples, meaning]) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{group}</th>
              <td>{examples}</td>
              <td>{meaning}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>
  <div class="summary-stack">
    <section class="summary-block summary-blue">
      <h2>This, that, these, those</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>This</strong> and <strong>that</strong> are for one thing. <strong>These</strong> and
        <strong>those</strong> are for more than one.
      </p>
      <p>this book, these books, that tree, those trees</p>
      <p>
        Near: this, these. Further away: that, those.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="summary-block summary-mint">
      <h2>Many, much and some</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Many</strong> is for things you can count: many apples. <strong>Much</strong> is for an
        amount: much water.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Some</strong> works with both: some apples, some water. <strong>Every</strong> and
        <strong>each</strong> point to the members one at a time: every child, each book.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="summary-block summary-yellow">
      <h2>Determiner or pronoun?</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Those books</strong> are mine. <em>Those</em> is a determiner: a noun follows.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Those</strong> are mine. <em>Those</em> is a pronoun: no noun follows.
      </p>
      <p>
        The same test works for <em>my coat</em> (determiner) and <em>mine</em> (pronoun).
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>
